"""
Open-loop pitch departure from trim.

Identical to `F16OpenLoopTrim` except that `theta_init` is nudged 1 degree above the
trim attitude and the horizon is long enough for the consequence to be unmistakable.

At the reference CG the F-16 is statically unstable in pitch (Cma = +0.082/rad), which
puts a real pole at roughly +0.09 rad/s — a perturbation doubles about every 7.6 s and
never comes back. Where `F16OpenLoopTrim` shows that the trim point is an equilibrium,
this shows that it is an unstable one, which is the reason the aircraft needs the
regulator designed in tutorial steps 3 and 4.

Set `plant.xcg = 0.30` to move the CG forward of the aerodynamic reference and watch
the same perturbation decay instead.

Signal flow: Constants -> Mux5 -> F16PlantModel
"""
test component F16OpenLoopDeparture
  # ---- Trim control inputs, held fixed: no pilot, no controller ----
  T_cmd   = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 10794.89)
  el_cmd  = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = -0.6949)
  ail_cmd = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 0.0)
  rud_cmd = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 0.0)
  lef_cmd = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 0.0)
  # ---- Signal routing ----
  mux = F16ModelWorkshop.Utils.Mux5()
  # ---- Plant, started 1 degree nose-up of the trim attitude ----
  plant = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel(
    alt_init = 3000.0, vt_init = 152.4,
    alpha_init = 0.059129, theta_init = 0.076582,
    beta_init = 0.0, phi_init = 0.0, psi_init = 0.0,
    P_init = 0.0, Q_init = 0.0, R_init = 0.0
  )
relations
  connect(T_cmd.y,   mux.u1)
  connect(el_cmd.y,  mux.u2)
  connect(ail_cmd.y, mux.u3)
  connect(rud_cmd.y, mux.u4)
  connect(lef_cmd.y, mux.u5)
  connect(mux.y, plant.u_in)
end

analysis F16OpenLoopDepartureAnalysis
  # 40 s: long enough that pitch has tripled and 22 m/s of airspeed is gone, short
  # enough that alpha stays inside the range the coefficient deck was fitted over.
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 40.0)
  model = F16OpenLoopDeparture()
end
